!! TidGi Filesystem Integration

TidGi uses the upstream `$:/plugins/tiddlywiki/filesystem` sync adaptor. This plugin contains only the application-specific integration that does not belong in TiddlyWiki core:

* an `nsfw` implementation of the upstream `filesystemwatcher` provider interface
* the `in-tagtree-of` filter operator used by TidGi workspace routing filters
* routing explanation utilities used by the TidGi UI

At boot, TidGi translates its main/sub-workspace model into an in-memory `tiddlywiki.files` specification. The upstream adaptor then owns file loading and saving, watcher event coalescing, self-write suppression, the reverse filepath index, locked-file retries, external attachment moves and dynamic-store routing.

TidGi subscribes to the upstream filesystem hooks for Git-log refreshes, native error reporting and its worker sync cadence. No filesystem sync adaptor is implemented or subclassed here.
